cmu-mohawk-gunnery-only = Fire the M90 from the dedicated gunnery console.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-seat = You must be buckled into the gunnery seat to fire the M90.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-manual = Take turret control
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-panel-title = GUNNERY CONTROL
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark = Mark target
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark-invalid = No visible valid target near the cursor. Squall requires a living entity; explosive ammunition can mark any entity.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-automatic = Release / close defense
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-resume-ai = Release / resume AI scanning
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-control-help = First calibrate the grounded M90 hardpoint with a screwdriver, then program your faction IFF with a multitool. The first console opening runs a ship-wide boot test with staged loading progress; repair faulted hardpoints locally with a multitool. Take control while seated and landed, in transit, or during a CAS flyby. PGU-410 Squall holds 1200 rounds, deals 41 piercing damage, and fires fifteen rounds per second (900 RPM). Ground aimpoints within the twenty-tile, 225-degree circle stop rounds at the cursor; outside the circle, rounds keep traveling until collision. Cameras and AR do not obey wall line of sight. Flybys and transit support all M90 ammunition: select an active signal flare on the right TARGET monitor for delayed impacts within ten tiles. Explosive shells fire three per second. Mouse aims; hold left click to fire. The turret slews at sixty degrees per second. WASD moves camera and turret. AR shows the firing radius in the main view. Mark then Authorize fire for thirty seconds for manual tracking. Ground AI auto-fires valid targets; airborne AI scanning requires APPROVE AI TARGET for every new lock. AI free fire stays enabled until toggled off; manual control pauses it. Disabling starts a five-minute cooldown. IFF can be toggled; disabling it removes friendly shot and impact protection. At zero integrity the M90 disables and requires a staged engineer rebuild.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ground-only = Manual chin-gun control requires landing, transit, or an active CAS flyby; it is unavailable during takeoff or tactical hover.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ammo-ground-only = This ammunition cannot be used while airborne. Select an airborne-compatible feed.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ammo-air-only = Explosive M90 ammunition is airborne-only. Select PGU-410 Squall for groundside fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-busy = Another operator is controlling the chin turret.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-out-of-range = The target is outside the chin turret's range.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-out-of-arc = The target is behind the chin turret's forward firing arc.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-auth-expired = Fire authorization expired. Confirm the target again to resume.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-unsafe-shot = Holding fire: a friendly or an opaque obstruction is in the firing path.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-flare-invalid = Flare targeting requires active flight and a selected active signal flare. Aim within ten tiles of that flare. Clearing the flare disables airborne fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark-help = Press this button, then click a visible target in the left camera. Squall can mark living entities; explosive ammunition can mark any entity. Marking never authorizes fire or bypasses friendly safety.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark-pending = Click a target in the left camera.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-unmarked = No marked target.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-acquire = Acquire priority target
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-acquire-help = Mark the nearest or highest-health visible hostile, according to the priority setting. With a flare selected, acquire only within ten tiles of it. Then authorize fire separately.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-authorize = Authorize fire (30 seconds)
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-authorize-help = Mark or acquire a target first. Authorizes that entity for thirty seconds, firing only while visible and safe.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-priority-distance = Priority: nearest
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-priority-health = Priority: highest health
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-clear-flare = Clear flare / recenter
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-pan-help = Pan two tiles with the arrows. The center button recenters on the flare or chin mount. Panning clears tracking and authorization.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-short-help = Mouse: aim | Hold click: fire
    Mark -> Authorize: tracked fire
    WASD / arrows: pan | AR: main view
    Airborne TARGET: select a flare
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airborne-flare-only = Airborne M90 fire requires airborne flight and a selected signal flare. Landed fire uses physical shells; tactical hover does not support flare fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airborne-preview = Airborne fire: ten tiles around the flare | Impact delay: 1-2 seconds | Squall: 15/s; explosive: 3/s
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airburst-blocked = Holding fire: the dispersed impact is outside the flare area, under protected cover, or too close to a friendly.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airburst-cancelled = A delayed M90 impact was cancelled because friendly clearance was lost. The released shell remains consumed.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-selected = Feed mode: selected
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-alternate = Feed mode: alternate each shell
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-select = Feed {$feed} {$active}
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-ammo = {$ammo} ({$rounds} rounds)
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-empty = empty
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-enable = Enable AI free fire scanning
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-disabled = M90 disabled: requires a complete rebuild.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-health = M90 integrity: {$health}/{$max} HP
cmu-mohawk-repair-grounded = The dropship must be grounded to rebuild the M90.
cmu-mohawk-repair-strip = Disabled M90: use a wrench to strip the damaged mechanism.
cmu-mohawk-repair-parts = Disabled M90: install one box of 90mm repair parts.
cmu-mohawk-repair-cable = Disabled M90: add ten lengths of cable.
cmu-mohawk-repair-weld = Disabled M90: weld the housing with a lit blowtorch (5 fuel).
cmu-mohawk-repair-calibrate = Disabled M90: calibrate and close it with a screwdriver.
cmu-mohawk-repair-complete = M90 rebuild complete: restored to 2000 HP and ready for operation.
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-active = Disable AI free fire scanning
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-cooldown = AI free fire cooldown: {$seconds}s
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-help = Enables continuous AI scanning until this button disables it. Ground targets are engaged automatically; airborne targets require individual gunner approval. Taking manual control pauses scanning without disabling it. While airborne the AI scans all active flares and chooses compatible feeds. Airborne approval ends when the target changes or becomes critical. Disabling starts a five-minute cooldown.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ar = AR mode
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ar-exit = Return to gun panel
cmu-mohawk-flare-warning = WARNING: M90 gunner locked onto a nearby signal flare. You are inside its ten-tile engagement area. Clear the area!
cmu-mohawk-setup-screw = M90 offline: use a screwdriver on its hardpoint to calibrate it.
cmu-mohawk-setup-iff = M90 calibrated: use a multitool on its hardpoint to program your faction IFF.
cmu-mohawk-setup-ready = M90 calibrated and faction IFF programmed. Ready for gunner control.
cmu-mohawk-setup-no-faction = IFF programming failed: no recognized faction identification was found.
cmu-mohawk-iff-on = IFF ENABLED
cmu-mohawk-iff-off = IFF DISABLED - FRIENDLY FIRE POSSIBLE
cmu-mohawk-ai-approve = APPROVE AI TARGET
cmu-mohawk-ai-revoke = REVOKE AI APPROVAL
